<!-- Added by Plutext Pty Ltd for the docx4j FO renderer (docx4j-fo-renderer), a modified distribution derived
     from Apache FOP 2.12: a paragraph of several sequences read again from a break between them (fop/CR-037). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      A paragraph that a preserved linefeed or a nested block divides into several sequences, read again from a break
      between two of them, goes on from there. It was read again from its first sequence, so its lines were drawn twice,
      or, at a change of page width, one was lost. Each sequence has six numbered lines, and each must be drawn once. a:
      a plain float's end edge. b: an offset float's start edge. c: the same, each line break a nested zero-height block,
      as docx4j writes a w:br. d: a plain float's end edge, the nested blocks holding a line of text, a sequence of one
      box that the restart must not take for empty. e: the next page narrower. f: the same, with nested blocks. g: an
      obstacle's band.
    </p>
  </info>
